# hotpot-iptv — example environment
#
# Copy to .env and edit:  cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored; this file is not. Keep real secrets out of it.
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS READ — every path below picks it up automatically, and in
# all of them a real exported environment variable overrides the file:
#   the app         config.Load() reads ./.env through viper's dotenv codec.
#   go test         pkg/testdb resolves PSQL_TEST_URL from the repo-root .env,
#                   so `go test -p 1 ./...` needs no setup. It looks from the
#                   repo root, not the CWD, because each test package runs in
#                   its own directory.
#   task            Taskfile.yml declares `dotenv: ['.env']`.
#   docker compose  reads ./.env itself for ${VAR} interpolation.
#
# Defaults below are the ones compiled into internal/config/config.go. Lines
# that are commented out are already the default — uncomment only to override.


# ─── Deployment secrets (docker compose) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Used by docker-compose.yml. The app never reads these directly; compose
# builds PSQL_URL from POSTGRES_PASSWORD and mounts the SMB share as /media.

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me

# Host port docker compose publishes the app on. The container always listens
# on 8080; change this when 8080 is already taken on the host.
#HTTP_PORT=8080

SMB_HOST=192.168.1.10
SMB_SHARE=media
SMB_USER=smbuser
SMB_PASSWORD=change-me


# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No default. If unset, main.go still serves /healthz and the library browser
# but does NOT mount the channels API — so set it for anything real.
# Under compose this is set from POSTGRES_PASSWORD against the `db` service;
# the value below is for running the binary on the host.

PSQL_URL=postgres://hotpot:change-me@localhost:5432/hotpot?sslmode=disable


# ─── HTTP ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#PORT=8080


# ─── Paths ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These defaults are container paths. Running on the host, point them at real
# directories — MEDIA_PATH is the library root (read-only is fine), STREAMS_PATH
# is where segment output is written and swept.
#MEDIA_PATH=/media
#STREAMS_PATH=/streams


# ─── HLS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WINDOW_SEGMENTS is the live sliding window; at 4s segments, 30 is ~2 minutes.
# It also bounds disk use: segments outside the window are deleted, and item
# directories below the oldest still-referenced one are swept.
#SEGMENT_SECONDS=4
#WINDOW_SEGMENTS=30


# ─── Encoding ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENCODER: nvenc | software
#   nvenc     -> h264_nvenc, for the Quadro M620 (Maxwell: H.264 only, no HEVC/AV1)
#   software  -> libx264, for GPU-less dev boxes and CI
#ENCODER=nvenc

#VIDEO_WIDTH=1920
#VIDEO_HEIGHT=1080
#VIDEO_BITRATE_K=5000


# ─── FFmpeg binaries ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Resolved on PATH by default. The Docker image sets absolute paths instead.
#FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg
#FFPROBE_PATH=ffprobe


# ─── Dev tooling only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both of these point at databases that get WIPED. Give each a dedicated
# database — never the real one in PSQL_URL.
#
# PSQL_DEV_URL: scratch database Atlas uses to compute the diff against
#   schema.hcl, for `task migrate-dev`. Atlas resets it on every run.
#   With Docker installed, Atlas can provision one itself:
#       PSQL_DEV_URL=docker://postgres/16/dev
#   Without Docker, point it at a real empty database you created for this —
#   and match your server's major version, not the 16 above:
#PSQL_DEV_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/hotpot_atlas_dev?sslmode=disable

# PSQL_TEST_URL: read by pkg/testdb, which DROPs and recreates every table on
#   each run. Defaults to a local Unix socket if unset:
#       postgres:///hotpot_test?host=/var/run/postgresql
#   Point it at a dedicated test database — a remote one is fine:
#PSQL_TEST_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/hotpot_test?sslmode=disable
